\subsection{VLA Robustness}

VLAs have progressed from tokenized action prediction~\cite{brohan2023rt2,kim2024openvla,ghosh2024octo} to generative action models based on diffusion~\cite{chi2023diffusion_policy} and flow matching~\cite{black2024pi0,shukor2025smolvla}, with the latter producing stochastic action samples that enable multi-sample inference strategies.
Improving VLA robustness divides into training-time and inference-time approaches.

However, multi-sampling is an enabling condition: at $K{=}1$, correction alone falls below baseline (10.3\% vs.\ 11.6\%), because the single sample lacks the centering that argmin selection provides within the CRM's bounded correction radius.
Per-seed variance is substantial: on seed 43, argmin selection (17\%) slightly outperforms obs\_only correction (16\%), though the seven-seed mean favors correction.

\paragraph{Spatial benchmark: correction does not help.}

